  "source_binding": "One unchanged final snapshot for full workspace checks, fixed release build and actual process acceptance. Includes all non-document crate/contract files, dependencies, toolchain, Rust gate and IPC validator.",
  "implementation": [
    "ObserveCurrent checkpoint queries preserve exact capture and pause semantics of previous modes. Each fresh response binds actual kernel process incarnation, authenticated session, unique challenge, report lower bound, actual READY and original deadline.",
    "Worker input callbacks continue while queries wait or replies are backpressured. A single response is retained without re-executing checkpoint; ordered control responses precede coalesced periodic announcements. A query also publishes its verified state through the ordinary READY path.",
    "Host brackets cold completion with actual owned Child/kernel/image/resource observations, rechecks the complete recovery closure and actual account report prefix/shared cursor, then samples the original deadline again. Closed challenges absorb known late replies; accepted request IDs are never reused within the bounded owner lifetime.",
    "App explicitly approves local private directories, UID, Binding and query-capable build hashes. Received requests are synced before dispatch; canonical shared dependencies and result CAS are synced before terminal WAL and atomic outbox publication.",
    "Recovery verifies every persisted dependency hash/length and READY root. Historical results retain original request/expiry; unfinished requests become Interrupted without dispatching a new worker challenge. Conflicting IDs cancel unfinished originals. Storage failure closes only the diagnostic provider.",
    "Whole-suite concurrency exposed inherited flock descriptions surviving clean owner drop. Private lock guards now explicitly unlock at the actual final owner boundary, including construction errors; legitimate shared Raft snapshot owners retain exclusion until their final Arc is dropped."
  ],
