  "limits": [
    "The provider observes one exact strategy instance at a time. Full global runtime projection application, revision/hash claims, signed host-wide RuntimeFacts and persistent source-watermark consumers remain unfinished.",
    "The external entry is authorized through approved local Linux directory/UID and Binding; it is not a remotely authenticated network API. Cross-UID deployment and actual delegated resource-group positive qualification remain unverified on this host.",
    "Observation and CAS verification/persistence are explicit cold work on the owner loop. Continuous worker callbacks and bounded queues do not establish production throughput or latency qualification.",
    "A Host keeps at most 4096 accepted request IDs, 4096 report prefixes per active query and 16 unanswered closed challenges. Expiry releases lane exclusion, but only a matching authenticated response removes its closed challenge; exhaustion rejects diagnostics without granting trading authority.",
    "The actual backpressure test consumes 176 account records and verifies the earlier queued query. Its final new query reaches the existing typed recovery 16MiB bound and is correctly rejected; this is not recorded as a successful fresh proof.",
    "The archived verifier checks captured bytes, request/process/binary bindings, signatures and independently recalculates account input prefixes. Large ELF/recovery CAS objects remain local; complete closure verification was run online against actual persisted objects, not reconstructed from this archive.",
    "The rebuild and App scenarios each record one startup Clock gap, followed by BeginReconciliation at epoch 2/generation 2 and an actual account_reconciled event before command registration. Historical gap counts are retained; this stage does not claim a gap-free run.",
    "Native WSL2 Linux and local TLS exchange fixtures only; no live Binance credentials or orders, no Docker check-linux run, no production qualification or measured latency claim.",
    "No TLC execution, model updates or historical lock rebasing. Source changes and missing historical paths are recorded by read-only anchor audit; new formal verification remains deferred until functional development is complete."
  ]
}
